#lang scribble/manual

@(require (for-label racket/base manifold/unsafe))

@title[#:tag "unsafe-reference"]{Exact C ABI}

@defmodule[manifold/unsafe]

This module exports every declaration from the targeted @tt{manifoldc.h} under
its exact underscore-separated C name, including @tt{manifold_cube},
@tt{manifold_alloc_manifold}, and @tt{manifold_delete_manifold}.
Signatures retain placement-memory pointers, raw arrays, callbacks, and manual
allocation or destruction.

The declarations are mechanically generated by
@filepath{scripts/generate-unsafe.py}. Use this module for ABI diagnostics,
foreign-pointer interoperation, or new upstream functionality that has not yet
received a managed spelling. Ordinary applications should use
@racketmodname[manifold] or @racketmodname[manifold/low-level].

Unsafe callers are responsible for allocating correctly sized native storage,
matching construction with destruction or deletion, keeping callback closures
reachable, and preventing use-after-free. No Layer 2 implementation imports
this module directly.
